  "problem": "If $U={2,4,6,8,10,12}$ is the universal set and $B={2,6,10},$ then the complement of $B$ is",
  "worked_solution": "The complement of $B,$ denoted $\\overset{\u2015}{B},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $B.$\n\nThe elements of $U$ that are not in $B$ are $4,$ $8,$   and $12.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $B$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{B}={4,8,12}.\n$$",
